# What the deployment does not need.
#
# The hosted app is pwa/ served by serve_pwa.py, and that is all. This file matters
# because a working copy that has ever built the old generation still holds several
# hundred megabytes of installer, PyInstaller output and node_modules on disk, and
# `railway up` uploads the directory rather than the commit.
#
# Ignored by .gitignore too, but stated here so an upload cannot depend on that.
dist-app/
dist-backend/
build-backend/
electron/
src-tauri/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.gradio/
node_modules/
.env

# Repository furniture, not runtime.
.git/
.github/
README.md
